      "Language": "eng",
      "Abstract": {"AbstractText": "Urinary tract infections (UTIs) are common in the elderly, yet there is much disagreement in the literature regarding many aspects of this condition. To assist the nurse in developing optimum care strategies, UTI criteria in the elderly are discussed. Using the most recent knowledge to guide clinical assessment and intervention skills, the longterm care facility nurse and nurses who care for the elderly can influence positive outcomes in this challenging population."},
